---
title: Japanese Sauerkraut (Tsukemono)
servings: 8
time: 3 days
tags: fermented, japanese, condiment, side-dish
cuisine: Japanese
course: side
source: Nourishing Traditions by Sally Fallon, p. 94 (001.jpg)
---

In a #large bowl{}, combine @Napa cabbage{1%head}(cored and shredded), @green onions{1%bunch}(chopped), @naturally fermented soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @fresh lemon juice{2%tbsp}, @sea salt{1%tsp}, and @whey{2%tbsp}(or 1 extra tsp sea salt).

Pound vigorously with a #wooden pounder{} or #meat hammer{} for 5 to 10 minutes to release the vegetable juices.

Transfer the mixture into a #quart-sized wide-mouth mason jar{} and press down firmly until the juices rise above the vegetables, leaving at least 1 inch of headspace below the rim.

Cover tightly and leave at room temperature for about ~{3%days} before transferring to cold storage.
